{"candidates":[{"content":"Strengthen the grounded extension by making validity-node closure an intrinsic derived property of the fixpoint rather than an enforcement in att construction: add a monotone closure operator that, at each pass, treats any attacker of a validity_node as attacking the warrant carrier, so the closure is re-derived by the same skeptical rule. Determinism and polynomial cost are preserved because the operator is monotone and idempotent, and validity of committed roots becomes a theorem of the fixpoint itself.","typicality":0.7,"evidence_refs":[{"block":"0974daebd1665965"},{"block":"0c302d11d621778b"}],"neighbours":["SRC_001"]},{"content":"Introduce a graded attack relation with a deterministically ordered threshold sweep: each attack edge carries strength in [0,1]; run the grounded fixpoint at k fixed thresholds in ascending order and accept a conjecture iff it is IN in every pass. The sweep order is part of the spec, so the result is deterministic and cost is k×polynomial; reinstatement is re-verified per threshold and remains derived. The open critique is that threshold choice is arbitrary and the intersection can be strictly less decisive than single-threshold grounded.","typicality":0.55,"evidence_refs":[{"block":"09ffabcd92979168"}],"neighbours":["SRC_001"]},{"content":"Reformulate reinstatement as a second-order recurrence over defense depth: a node is IN at pass n iff all its attackers are OUT at pass n−1 and at least one fully IN defense chain of length ≥2 exists at pass n−2. Labels are a linear recurrence over the same graph, so determinism and polynomial cost hold, but the semantics is strictly more decisive than standard grounded in densely defended regions and is no longer Dung grounded — a genuine semantics change, not an extension.","typicality":0.3,"evidence_refs":[{"block":"0e806619395ec8f4"},{"block":"0c302d11d621778b"}],"neighbours":["SRC_001"]},{"content":"Add a committed-root checkpoint that does not alter the fixpoint: before any root is committed, verify the set of committed roots is conflict-free and every committed root is defended by already-committed roots; any root whose only defenders are UNDEC is held suspended. Determinism and polynomial cost are untouched since this is a post-check on a subset of nodes, and committed-root validity becomes an explicit, machine-checkable invariant rather than an implicit property.","typicality":0.65,"evidence_refs":[{"block":"0d20320ff9938143"},{"block":"1dd041117ca8c54a"}],"neighbours":["SRC_001"]},{"content":"Replace grounded extension with ideal semantics as the skeptical operator: the ideal extension is the maximal admissible set contained in every preferred extension — unique, skeptical, and strictly more decisive than grounded — and is computable in polynomial time via iterated grounded-extension calls on the reduced framework. Determinism is preserved; the cost is the re-derivation of reinstatement and committed-root validity as theorems of the new semantics, and the loss of the simple two-label fixpoint story.","typicality":0.25,"evidence_refs":[{"block":"09ffabcd92979168"},{"block":"0c302d11d621778b"}],"neighbours":["SRC_001"]},{"content":"Keep the fixpoint untouched but attach a blocking frontier to every suspended node: instead of a single UNDEC label, carry the set of attackers that are themselves UNDEC and jointly block the node; the frontier is computed in the same pass at no asymptotic cost, is deterministic, and gives adjudicators a targeted, citable reason for suspension without changing acceptance. The critique is that this enriches observability, not the extension's decisiveness.","typicality":0.85,"evidence_refs":[{"block":"09ffabcd92979168"}],"neighbours":["SRC_001"]}],"scratch_proposal":{"new_blocks":[{"local_key":"NEW_001","body":{"content":"Speculative: a two-layer fixpoint where the att graph and the dep graph are solved jointly — a node is OUT if it has an attacker that is IN in the att-layer OR if its dep set contains an OUT dependency; IN requires all attackers OUT and all dependencies IN. This is a monotone operator over the product lattice, so a unique least fixpoint exists and cost stays polynomial (monotone over a finite lattice, O(n^2) passes). The catch: joint reinstatement could let a weakly-attacked node ride on a strong dependency chain, so committed-root validity would need a new proof. The real question is whether dep should be allowed to reinforce IN at all, or only to constrain.","why_keep_this":"Captures the most promising direction for strengthening skepticism by coupling the two relations, while flagging the validity risk.","possible_next_move":"Test on the corpus whether the joint fixpoint changes any committed verdict on a replay.","unfinished":"Prove monotonicity of the joint operator and bound the number of passes.","bears_on_refs":["SRC_001"]}}],"unresolved_questions":[{"question":"Is there a monotone operator whose least fixpoint is strictly more decisive than grounded but still polynomial, and whose reinstatement is derived rather than imposed?","related_refs":["NEW_001"]},{"question":"Does adding a graded attack threshold break the 'validity of every committed root' invariant in any corpus replay?","related_refs":[]}]}}